{"p": "Our math: Orange is up 130% since 2015 ($20 to $45.99), Blue 84% since 2016 ($25 to $45.99) and Orange & Blue 52% ($40 to $60.99), before local fees. The Verge called the 2022 increase \"the fourth time in five years\" and noted Sling promised not to raise prices in 2020 and kept that promise. In 2024 The Verge listed the combo at \"$61\"; sling.com lists $60.99. For the 2026 change, Cord Cutters News reported: \"The price hike will impact current customers on their next bill after February 20th, 2026, and new customers starting today.\""},
{"p": "The other direction: the two $19.99 plans are new. Sling Select launched in August 2025 (\"For the first time since Sling launched 10 years ago, we’re introducing an all-new package\") and Sling Essentials on April 9, 2026 (Variety), so the cheapest way into paid Sling is now $19.99 rather than $45.99."},
{"h": "Sling TV vs YouTube TV on price"},
{"p": "Sling's biggest plan is still far cheaper than YouTube TV's main plan ($82.99 a month in November 2026; see our [YouTube TV price guide](" + YT + ")): Orange & Blue is $60.99, or $69.99 with all three locals. The trade-off is local channels. Every YouTube TV plan, even its Sports Plan, comes with your local channels; Sling has locals only in a limited number of big markets and never on Orange. Sling's lighter plans also limit streams: one on Orange and Essentials versus three on YouTube TV. Our math for a sports fan: Orange plus Sports Extra is $56.99, against $64.99 for YouTube TV's Sports Plan."},
